# Payer wallet private key (0x-prefixed 32-byte hex).
# Stub mode: any valid throwaway key — no funds required. See the README for a
# one-liner to generate one (ethers Wallet.createRandom or cast wallet new).
# Real settlement: a funded testnet key you control — never a key with meaningful
# funds. Leave the placeholder as 0x... until you paste your own; do not reuse a
# well-known demo key if you will fund the address later.
PRIVATE_KEY=0x...

# Source-chain RPC URL (Base Sepolia). Needed only for real settlement, where the
# client approves the source token (Permit2) before signing. Leave blank for the stub.
#   RPC_URL=https://sepolia.base.org
RPC_URL=

# Merchant URL defaults to the sibling example at http://localhost:4020/paid.
# Uncomment to point elsewhere.
#   MERCHANT_URL=http://localhost:4020/paid

# There is deliberately no PURCHASE_ID here. Each run generates and prints a fresh
# purchase id, so every run is a new payment. Pass it on the command line only to
# re-attempt a payment that was interrupted while still settling:
#   PURCHASE_ID=<the id the run printed> npm run pay
# Setting it here instead would make every run re-attempt the same payment, and later runs
# would be served without paying. See "Retries and idempotency" in the README.
